# The bit aot-profile options cd.bbscanner.demo.yml collects the deployed demo's profile with: bit aot-profile
# @src/Utilities/BbScanner/Demo/aot-profile.rsp, from the repository root, followed by the -o and -p options of the publish
# that compiles with the profile.
#
# A page the profile never ran mixes compiled and interpreted framework code in the AOT build, and Mono can stop the app
# there with an assertion at interp.c, as it stopped the Bmage demo's editor (#15100). So every page is visited, not just
# the start page bit aot-profile visits by default; bit warns if --max-pages leaves any out.
#
# A page only loaded runs what it renders, so the steps then scan a picked image on the image page, through Blazor's
# InputFile and through the scanner's own file input: the file read and the interop byte[] marshalling. The camera pages
# can't open a camera in the headless browser, which is why their scanning isn't stepped through.

src/Utilities/BbScanner/Demo/Server/Bit.BbScanner.Demo.Server.csproj
--max-pages 50
--include Bit.BbScanner
--step /image
--step "file:src/Utilities/BbScanner/Demo/Server/wwwroot/icon-512.png|#scan-image-input"
--step "file:src/Utilities/BbScanner/Demo/Server/wwwroot/icon-512.png|.bit-bbscanner input[type=file]"
